+## Acceptance result
+
+Two fresh non-local clones at source commit `e8bd954a1985e0a3204504209f1b022f71e4d1f9`, with independent work/cache/output roots and only the declared release-recipe overlay, reproduced every declared byte. All four relay executables, all four protocol-test executables, four SPDX documents, the four-entry manifest, checksum file, notices, and normalized four-member archive matched. No irreducible or unexplained variance remains, and no semantic-identity exception is used.
+
+The SPDX repair is appropriately narrow: real Syft reruns differed only at the generated `documentNamespace` in this review (both happened within the same timestamp second), and all other fields were byte-semantically equal. The recipe replaces only `documentNamespace` and `creationInfo.created`, derives the namespace from canonical executable name plus exact executable SHA-256, derives time from `SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH`, recursively sorts JSON object keys without reordering arrays, then verifies and hashes the exact generated bytes. Runtime bytes are already controlled by `-trimpath`, `-buildvcs=false`, `-s -w`, empty Go build ID, internal linking, fixed target baselines, pinned inputs, isolated caches, `LC_ALL=C`, `LANG=C`, and `TZ=UTC`.
+
+The comparator fits the existing release architecture: it validates the exact release/test tree, rejects symlinks and unsupported entries, compares modes and SHA-256, and reports bounded first-byte offsets plus semantic JSON paths where applicable. The normalized archive independently matched canonical member order, mode `0755`, uid/gid `0`, `root/root`, mtime `1787158980`, USTAR regular-file type, and empty PAX headers. Filesystem mtimes outside the archive are non-semantic; the consumer/checksum contract binds exact file bytes.
